# Agent prompts & skills

The base agent system prompts must stay **lean**. They carry only universal
directives, workflow, discovery strategy, engine mapping, console management,
the tool list, and pointers to skills. Everything that is vendor-, database-,
app-, or domain-specific belongs in an **Agent Skill**, never the base prompt.

## Where things live

- Base prompts (lean): [api/src/agent-lib/prompts/universal.ts](mdc:api/src/agent-lib/prompts/universal.ts), [api/src/agents/unified/prompt.ts](mdc:api/src/agents/unified/prompt.ts).
- System skills (heavy reference, loaded on demand): [api/src/agent-skills/](mdc:api/src/agent-skills/) — one `SKILL.md` package per capability. See [api/src/agent-skills/README.md](mdc:api/src/agent-skills/README.md).
- Registry + discovery: [api/src/agent-lib/skills/system-skills.ts](mdc:api/src/agent-lib/skills/system-skills.ts).
- Retrieval/injection pipeline (shared with workspace skills): [api/src/services/skills.service.ts](mdc:api/src/services/skills.service.ts).
- Tools: `load_skill` and `read_skill_resource` in [api/src/agent-lib/tools/skill-tools.ts](mdc:api/src/agent-lib/tools/skill-tools.ts).

## Rules

- **Do not add new vendor/database/app/domain guidance to a base prompt.** Create or extend an `api/src/agent-skills/<name>/SKILL.md` package instead.
- The skill's `description` frontmatter is the **retrieval trigger** ("when to load this skill"), written as a task/condition — not a summary.
- Keep the `SKILL.md` **body under ~500 lines**. Push long-form material into `references/*.md` and reference it from the body.
- **No duplication** between the body and references; each fact lives in one place.
- **One skill per capability** — don't bundle unrelated topics into a single package.
- When a standalone agent needs the full guide inlined, source it from the registry (`getSystemSkillFullText(name)`) rather than duplicating a literal, so there is one source of truth.
- Dynamic content (e.g. auto-generated form-field docs) uses `{{PLACEHOLDER}}` tokens substituted via `registerSystemSkillTemplate(name, provider)` at module load.
- A new skill is auto-discovered at boot — no registration code needed beyond creating the package directory and `SKILL.md`.

## Why

Always-on reference bloat made the base system prompt very large (every chat
turn paid for every dialect, the full dashboard guide, and the full flow guide).
Skills move that to progressive disclosure: the catalog (name + description) is
always injected, but bodies and references load only when relevant.
